    "md5": "dafd2c7f641a8f953f1534d25c14c8c4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1734,
    "chunk_text": "Jaffna Bar Association calls for probe into transfer of High Court Judge\n\nJaffna, June 01 (Daily Mirror) - The Bar Association of Jaffna has called on President Anura Kumara Dissanayake to urgently investigate the transfer of Jaffna High Court Judge A. G. Alexraja, raising concerns over possible interference with judicial independence.\n\nThe Jaffna Bar Association stated that Judge Alexraja was appointed to the Jaffna High Court on April 22, 2026, and was subsequently transferred to the Civil Appellate High Court in Badulla within little more than a month of assuming office. The transfer is scheduled to take effect from May 31, 2026.\n\nIn a letter addressed to the President, the Association said the request was made following a resolution adopted at its Extraordinary General Meeting held on May 29, 2026.\n\nAccording to the Jaffna Bar Association, the sudden nature of the transfer has sparked speculation regarding the existence of reasons unrelated to the normal administrative process.\n\nThe Jaffna Bar Association further stated that it had received information from members suggesting that the transfer may have been linked to certain interim orders issued by Judge Alexraja in writ petitions where the Governor of the Northern Province had been named as a respondent.\n\n\u201cWe also have reliably heard from our membership that the transfer may have been occasioned by certain interim orders that the Honourable Judge had made against the Governor of the Northern Province,\u201d the letter stated.\n\nThe Association further claimed that it had received information indicating that the Governor had communicated with certain authorities, including members of the Government, seeking their intervention in relation to the matter."
